    ["<Assistant_Title1>[Voice Room - Gameplay Voice Room]</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Open Level: </>Cognitive Level <Assistant_Red>10</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Entry: </><Assistant_System>Chat Panel - Voice Room</>{JumpToUI:[[View]]|1250316}\n<Assistant_Title2>Capacity Limit: </>Voice rooms can accommodate up to 1000 people.\n<Assistant_Title2>Default Speaking Mode: </>Gameplay voice rooms default to the room owner setting the speaking order. You need to click the mic button to initiate a request to speak, and you can only unmute after the room owner approves.\n<Assistant_Title2>Heartbeat Signal: </>Players in the speaking queue automatically gain guest status; the player in the 1st mic position is the guest of honor. All guests in the voice room can express emotions by switching their \"light-up\" status. You can view the speaking and light-up status of all current guests more intuitively through the live interface in the top right corner of the room.\n<Assistant_Title2>Room Owner Operations: </>The room owner can adjust the speaking order, set mutes, and manage the room blacklist in the member permission settings. They can also adjust room information, extend the duration of permanent rooms, and transfer ownership in the settings interface on the right sidebar.\n<Assistant_Title2>Other Operations: </>You can share the voice room link and distribute voice room gifts in the right sidebar.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Voice Room - Owner Permissions]|1395}, {SendAnswer:[Voice Room - Normal Voice Room]|1396}, {SendAnswer:[Voice Room - Permanent Room]|1398}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>[Voice Room - Gameplay Voice Room]</>\n<Assistant_Title2>Open Level: </>Cognitive Level <Assistant_Red>10</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Entry: </><Assistant_System>Chat Panel - Voice Room</>{JumpToUI:[[View]]|1250316}\n<Assistant_Title2>Capacity Limit: </>Voice rooms can accommodate up to 1000 people.\n<Assistant_Title2>Default Speaking Mode: </>Gameplay voice rooms default to the room owner setting the speaking order. You need to click the mic button to initiate a request to speak, and you can only unmute after the room owner approves.\n<Assistant_Title2>Heartbeat Signal: </>Players in the speaking queue automatically gain guest status; the player in the 1st mic position is the guest of honor. All guests in the voice room can express emotions by switching their \"light-up\" status. You can view the speaking and light-up status of all current guests more intuitively through the live interface in the top right corner of the room.\n<Assistant_Title2>Room Owner Operations: </>The room owner can adjust the speaking order, set mutes, and manage the room blacklist in the member permission settings. They can also adjust room information, extend the duration of permanent rooms, and transfer ownership in the settings interface on the right sidebar.\n<Assistant_Title2>Other Operations: </>You can share the voice room link and distribute voice room gifts in the right sidebar.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Voice Room - Owner Permissions]|1395}, {SendAnswer:[Voice Room - Normal Voice Room]|1396}, {SendAnswer:[Voice Room - Permanent Room]|1398}",
