    ["April 12, 1345 \n First time touching father's tools. The hammer was heavier than expected, my hand shook so much I deformed the silver sheet. \n\n August 3, 1345 \n Learned to distinguish between rubies and garnets. \n\n February 18, 1346 \n Mother's cough worsened. Weekly wage rose to 12 sous, bought some throat-soothing herbs. \n\n July 9, 1346 \n Independently finished polishing a silver ring. The client was a dock worker, for his fiancée. \n\n March 15, 1347 \n Officially became a craftsman's apprentice. Father said my hands are steady, suitable for this trade. \n\n November 2, 1347 \n Learned to set moonstones. Father nodded. \n\n June 3, 1348 \n Weekly wage rose to 1 pound 5 sous. Mother made meat stew. \n\n September 14, 1348 \n First custom order. Customer wanted a brooch with an apple pattern, said it was for his wife. Drew the sketch three times before he was satisfied. \n\n January 20, 1349 \n Sorting through old items in the shop, found a yellowed family tree. Some names were crossed out. \n\n March 8, 1349 \n Mother's herbal powder is almost gone. Need to take more repair jobs this week. \n\n June 28, 1349 \n Received a strange notebook. Opened the first page, those symbols... I feel like I've seen them somewhere."] = "April 12, 1345 \n First time touching father's tools. The hammer was heavier than expected, my hand shook so much I deformed the silver sheet. \n\n August 3, 1345 \n Learned to distinguish between rubies and garnets. \n\n February 18, 1346 \n Mother's cough worsened. Weekly wage rose to 12 sous, bought some throat-soothing herbs. \n\n July 9, 1346 \n Independently finished polishing a silver ring. The client was a dock worker, for his fiancée. \n\n March 15, 1347 \n Officially became a craftsman's apprentice. Father said my hands are steady, suitable for this trade. \n\n November 2, 1347 \n Learned to set moonstones. Father nodded. \n\n June 3, 1348 \n Weekly wage rose to 1 pound 5 sous. Mother made meat stew. \n\n September 14, 1348 \n First custom order. Customer wanted a brooch with an apple pattern, said it was for his wife. Drew the sketch three times before he was satisfied. \n\n January 20, 1349 \n Sorting through old items in the shop, found a yellowed family tree. Some names were crossed out. \n\n March 8, 1349 \n Mother's herbal powder is almost gone. Need to take more repair jobs this week. \n\n June 28, 1349 \n Received a strange notebook. Opened the first page, those symbols... I feel like I've seen them somewhere.",
    ["<Assistant_Title1> [Friends - Cross-Server Friends] </>\n<Assistant_Title2> System Entry: </><Assistant_System> Menu - Friends - Cross-Server Friends </>\n<Assistant_Title2> Adding Friends: </><Assistant_System> Under the Friends - Add tab, enter the character nickname or character numeric ID to search for and add cross-server friends. </>\n Friend Gifting: <Assistant_Title2> You can use </> Friends - Private Chat - Gifting in the bottom right corner <Assistant_System> to exchange gifts with cross-server friends and increase friendliness. </>\n Recommended Searches: <Assistant_Title3></>, {SendAnswer:[好友]|1406}, {SendAnswer:[好友-好友列表]|1407}, {SendAnswer:[好友-私聊]|1408}, {SendAnswer:[好友-群聊]|1409}, {SendAnswer:[好友-好友度]|1410}, {SendAnswer:[好友-删除拉黑]|1412}"] = "<Assistant_Title1> [Friends - Cross-Server Friends] </>\n<Assistant_Title2> System Entry: </><Assistant_System> Menu - Friends - Cross-Server Friends </>\n<Assistant_Title2> Adding Friends: </><Assistant_System> Under the Friends - Add tab, enter the character nickname or character numeric ID to search for and add cross-server friends. </>\n Friend Gifting: <Assistant_Title2> You can use </> Friends - Private Chat - Gifting in the bottom right corner <Assistant_System> to exchange gifts with cross-server friends and increase friendliness. </>\n Recommended Searches: <Assistant_Title3></>, {SendAnswer:[Friends]|1406}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Friend List]|1407}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Private Chat]|1408}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Group Chat]|1409}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Friendliness]|1410}, {SendAnswer:[Friends - Delete/Block]|1412}",
